-- Regulation of Engagement in Work on Refrigeration or Air-Conditioning Systems (Fees) Regulations, 5785-2025
-- תקנות הסדרת העיסוק בעבודה במערכת קירור או מיזוג אוויר (אגרות), התשפ"ה-2025
-- Made under ss.59 and 60 of the Law. Kovetz HaTakanot 5785 p. 2116 (issue 11951); signed
-- 6 July 2025, published 9 July 2025, in force 16 July 2025 (reg. 5).
-- Amended by Kovetz HaTakanot 12383 of 4 May 2026, 5786 p. 2062 (signed 28 April
-- 2026 by Yariv Levin), which defined the theoretical examination, inserted
-- reg. 2(a1) for it and moved the appeal fee onto it.
--
-- THREE VINTAGES of regulation 2 are encoded side by side, because the same
-- test table is run against all three:
--   * the draft, exactly as shown in Figure 4 of Schwartz, Bar-Siman-Tov &
--     Gelbard, "When Computers Speak Laws" (Law, Society & Culture 8, 2025),
--     a screen capture of the SimpLEX drafting-and-testing tool;
--   * the Regulations as made in July 2025;
--   * the Regulations as amended in 5786.
-- Regulations 3 (indexation), 4 (payment as a precondition) and 5
-- (commencement) are encoded once; they did not change.
@lang en

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

§ `Chapter A -- Definitions`
§§ `reg. 1 Definitions`

-- "בחינה עיונית" -- the theoretical examination; "בחינה מעשית" -- the practical
-- examination: the two halves of the examination the Division of Vocational
-- Training sets for the completion certificate under s.2 of the Law.
DECLARE Service IS ONE OF
    `theoretical examination`
    `practical examination`
    `appeal against a theoretical examination score`
    `appeal against a practical examination score`
    `issue or renewal of a licence`             -- under s.5 of the Law
    `temporary licence for a foreign expert`    -- application or renewal under s.9 of the Law

DECLARE Vintage IS ONE OF
    `the SimpLEX draft`
    `the Regulations as made`
    `the Regulations as amended`

§ `Chapter B -- Fees`
§§ `reg. 2 Fees -- the draft as shown in SimpLEX`

-- Figure 4 reads, in translation:
--   (a) for a theoretical examination, a fee of 273 new shekels;
--   (b) for a practical examination, a fee of 194 new shekels;
--   (c) where an appeal is lodged against the result of a theoretical or a
--       practical examination, 40 new shekels per appeal, in addition to the
--       fee under (a);
--   (d) for an application to receive or renew a licence under s.5 of the Law,
--       284 new shekels;
--   (e) for an application for a temporary licence for a foreign expert under
--       "s.8 of the Law" [sic -- s.9 in the bill and the Act], 398 new shekels.
GIVEN service IS A Service
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the fee prescribed by the draft for` @nlg the fee the SimpLEX draft prescribes for %service%, in new shekels, if any
                                            @nlg:he האגרה שהטיוטה שבצילום המסך קובעת בעד %service%, בשקלים חדשים, אם נקבעה
    IS CONSIDER service
       WHEN `theoretical examination`                    THEN JUST 273   -- draft 2(a)
       WHEN `practical examination`                      THEN JUST 194   -- draft 2(b)
       WHEN `appeal against a theoretical examination score` THEN JUST 40 -- draft 2(c)
       WHEN `appeal against a practical examination score`   THEN JUST 40 -- draft 2(c)
       WHEN `issue or renewal of a licence`              THEN JUST 284   -- draft 2(d)
       WHEN `temporary licence for a foreign expert`     THEN JUST 398   -- draft 2(e)

§§ `reg. 2 Fees -- as made, Kovetz HaTakanot 5785 p. 2116`

-- Read from the gazette issue, Kovetz HaTakanot 11951 of 9 July 2025, p. 2116:
-- (a) for a practical examination, the candidate shall pay a fee of 194 new shekels;
-- (b) where an appeal is lodged against THE examination score, the appellant
--     shall pay, in addition to the fee under subregulation (a), 40 new shekels
--     per appeal;
-- (c) for the receipt or renewal of a licence under s.5 of the Law, 284 new shekels;
-- (d) for an application for a temporary licence for a foreign expert, or its
--     renewal, under s.9 of the Law, 398 new shekels.
-- Regulation 1 as made defined only "בחינה מעשית", the practical examination, so
-- "the examination" in (b) can only be that one, and (b) says so itself by
-- pointing at (a). The theoretical examination appears nowhere in the text as
-- made: no fee, and no appeal fee.
GIVEN service IS A Service
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the fee prescribed by the Regulations as made for` @nlg the fee the Regulations as made in July 2025 prescribe for %service%, in new shekels, if any
                                                          @nlg:he האגרה שהתקנות כנוסחן עם התקנתן ביולי 2025 קובעות בעד %service%, בשקלים חדשים, אם נקבעה
    IS CONSIDER service
       WHEN `theoretical examination`                    THEN NOTHING    -- no such item
       WHEN `practical examination`                      THEN JUST 194   -- 2(a)
       WHEN `appeal against a theoretical examination score` THEN NOTHING -- no such examination in the text as made
       WHEN `appeal against a practical examination score`   THEN JUST 40 -- 2(b), "in addition to the fee under (a)"
       WHEN `issue or renewal of a licence`              THEN JUST 284   -- 2(c)
       WHEN `temporary licence for a foreign expert`     THEN JUST 398   -- 2(d)

§§ `reg. 2 Fees -- as amended, Kovetz HaTakanot 5786 p. 2062`

-- The amendment added a definition of "בחינה עיונית" to reg. 1, inserted
-- (a1) -- for a theoretical examination, 158 new shekels --
-- and rewrote (b): the appeal fee now attaches to the THEORETICAL examination
-- score, "in addition to the fee under (a1)". So the appeal fee moved from the
-- practical examination to the theoretical one. Everything else as made.
GIVEN service IS A Service
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the fee prescribed by the Regulations as amended for` @nlg the fee the Regulations as amended in 5786 prescribe for %service%, in new shekels, if any
                                                             @nlg:he האגרה שהתקנות כנוסחן לאחר תיקון התשפ״ו קובעות בעד %service%, בשקלים חדשים, אם נקבעה
    IS CONSIDER service
       WHEN `theoretical examination`                        THEN JUST 158  -- 2(a1)
       WHEN `appeal against a theoretical examination score` THEN JUST 40   -- 2(b) as amended
       WHEN `appeal against a practical examination score`   THEN NOTHING   -- 2(b) as amended reaches the theoretical score only
       OTHERWISE `the fee prescribed by the Regulations as made for` service

@export The fee, in new shekels, that the Fees Regulations prescribe for a service, under a chosen vintage of the text; NOTHING means no fee is prescribed
GIVEN vintage IS A Vintage  @desc which text to read: the SimpLEX draft, the Regulations as made (July 2025), or as amended (5786)
      service IS A Service  @desc the service the fee is charged for
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the fee under` @nlg the fee under %vintage% for %service%
                      @nlg:he האגרה לפי %vintage% בעד %service%
    IS CONSIDER vintage
       WHEN `the SimpLEX draft`          THEN `the fee prescribed by the draft for` service
       WHEN `the Regulations as made`    THEN `the fee prescribed by the Regulations as made for` service
       WHEN `the Regulations as amended` THEN `the fee prescribed by the Regulations as amended for` service

§§ `reg. 3 Updating of fees`

-- (a) The fee amounts in reg. 2 are updated on 1 January of each year (the
--     update day) by the rate of change of the new index against the base
--     index, and rounded to the nearest whole new shekel; for this purpose --
--     "the new index": the index published in the November before the update day;
--     "the base index": the index published in the November before the previous
--     update day, and for the first update day after these Regulations commence,
--     the index published in the month before they commenced;
--     "index": the consumer price index published by the Central Bureau of Statistics.
-- Rounding at exactly one half is not settled by the text; half-up is adopted
-- (fork F2 in NOTES.md).
GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`rounded to the nearest whole shekel` x MEANS FLOOR (x PLUS 0.5)

@export A fee amount after the annual 1 January update under regulation 3: scaled by the consumer price index and rounded to the nearest whole new shekel
GIVEN fee IS A NUMBER          @desc the fee amount before the update, in new shekels
      `new index` IS A NUMBER  @desc the CPI published in the November before the update day
      `base index` IS A NUMBER @desc the CPI published in the November before the previous update day (or the month before commencement, for the first update)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the updated fee` @nlg the fee of %fee% shekels updated by the ratio of the index %`new index`% to the base index %`base index`%, rounded to the nearest shekel
                        @nlg:he האגרה בסך %fee% שקלים חדשים מעודכנת לפי שיעור השינוי של המדד החדש %`new index`% לעומת המדד היסודי %`base index`%, ומעוגלת לשקל החדש השלם הקרוב
    IS `rounded to the nearest whole shekel` (fee TIMES `new index` DIVIDED BY `base index`)

§§ `reg. 4 Payment of the fee as a condition of a licence or an examination`

-- The registrar shall not grant or renew a licence for which a fee is prescribed,
-- and the Division shall not allow the examinations or an appeal for which a fee
-- is prescribed, unless the applicant has paid that fee in full.
-- Where NO fee is prescribed for the service, reg. 4 has nothing to bite on.
-- The appeal fee is "in addition to" the examination fee: the appellant's total
-- outlay is 198 as amended, of which 158 bought the examination. `paid` here is
-- the amount paid toward the fee for THIS service, so an appeal is 40.
-- reg. 3(b), the Director-General's duty to publish the updated reg. 2 in
-- Reshumot, is not modelled.
@export Whether the registrar or the Division of Vocational Training may provide a service, given what the applicant has paid, under regulation 4 and a chosen vintage of regulation 2
GIVEN vintage IS A Vintage  @desc which text of regulation 2 to read
      service IS A Service  @desc the service applied for
      paid    IS A NUMBER   @desc the amount the applicant has paid toward the fee, in new shekels
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the service may be provided` @nlg %service% may be provided under %vintage% to an applicant who has paid %paid% shekels
                                    @nlg:he ניתן לתת את %service% לפי %vintage% למבקש הרישיון או השירות ששילם %paid% שקלים חדשים
    IF CONSIDER `the fee under` vintage service
       WHEN NOTHING  THEN TRUE
       WHEN JUST fee THEN paid AT LEAST fee

§§ `reg. 5 Commencement`

GIVEN published IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `the Regulations commence on` @nlg the Regulations commence seven days after their publication on %published%
                                    @nlg:he תחילתן של התקנות שבעה ימים מיום פרסומן ביום %published%
    IS published PLUS 7

§ `Illustrations`

#EVAL `the fee under` `the Regulations as amended` `theoretical examination`
#ASSERT `the updated fee` 194 105.3 104.1 EQUALS 196
#ASSERT `the updated fee` 284 105.3 104.1 EQUALS 287
#ASSERT `the updated fee` 398 105.3 104.1 EQUALS 403
#ASSERT `the Regulations commence on` (YMD 2025 7 9) EQUALS YMD 2025 7 16
